  "id": "DrugBank_DB00634 - MONDO_2289",
  "verbalization": "Sulfacetamide is implicated in the pathogenesis of Iris Disease through a chain of indications that ultimately converge on Prednisolone Acetate, which in turn links to Iris Disease. The evidence suggests that Sulfacetamide may contribute to the development of Ciliary Body Disease or Iridocyclitis, both of which are associated with Rimexolone, a corticosteroid that is also linked to Iris Disease. This suggests a potential mechanism where Sulfacetamide could influence inflammatory processes that lead to ocular conditions involving the ciliary body or iridocyclitis, which in turn may predispose to Iris Disease. The indirect relationship is supported by the cumulative evidence across the three paths, with the shared role of Rimexolone and Prednisolone Acetate as mediators. The strength of the evidence is reinforced by the overlapping indications and the sequential pathways, though the exact mechanism by which Sulfacetamide influences these conditions remains to be elucidated.",
